:["JuJu & Jordache","Juju","Juju And Jordash","Juju&Jordash","Juju, Jordash"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/300774-Juju-Jordash","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/pages/Juju-Jordash/88024840603","http://www.myspace.com/jujujordash","http://soundcloud.com/jujujordash"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3101/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3101","image":"https://i.discogs.com/UHxIjtn_cOgE8fJk893nhhuQBxVRhpW9nUNKamE4XL8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:400/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMxMDEt/MTczNTk4NjkyNS0z/NjE5LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/b_339oQt0X5g7E6Pfj2K7aBLcyMwzvmleMYQZbg55pc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMxMDEt/MTczNTk4NjkyNS0z/NjE5LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Born in the UK as Quentin Leo Cook on 31 July 1963. Was married to radio DJ & television presenter Zoë Ball, thus son-in-law of British television personality [a=Johnny Ball].\r\n \r\nCook adopted the new pseudonym Fatboy Slim in 1995. The Fatboy Slim album and Cook's second solo album Better Living Through Chemistry (released through Skint Records) contained the Top 40 UK hit, \"Everybody Needs a 303\".\r\nFatboy Slim's next work was the single \"The Rockafeller Skank\", released prior to the album You've Come a Long Way, Baby, both of which were released in 1998. \"Praise You\", also from this album, was Cook's first UK solo number one. Its music video, starring Spike Jonze, won numerous awards.\r\nIn 2000, Fatboy Slim released his third studio album, Halfway Between the Gutter and the Stars, and featured two collaborations with Macy Gray and \"Weapon of Choice\", which also was made into an award-winning video starring Christopher Walken.\r\nIn 2003, he produced Crazy Beat and Gene by Gene from the Blur album Think Tank, and in 2004, Palookaville was Cook's first studio album for four years.\r\nFatboy Slim's greatest hits album Why Try Harder was released on 19 June 2006. It comprises eighteen tracks, including ten Top 40 singles, a couple of Number Ones and two exclusive new tracks – \"Champion Sound\" and \"That Old Pair of Jeans\".","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3101","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":9050,"name":"Norman Cook"},{"id":21577,"name":"The Feelgood Factor"},{"id":30249,"name":"Urban All Stars"},{"id":53587,"name":"Sunny Side Up"},{"id":53588,"name":"Yum Yum Head Food"},{"id":86128,"name":"Chemistry (4)"},{"id":89450,"name":"Son Of A Cheeky Boy"},{"id":230148,"name":"Cheeky Boy"},{"id":695011,"name":"Attack Hamster"},{"id":5384245,"name":"Charlie Stains"},{"id":7078732,"name":"Quentox"},{"id":16935259,"name":"D.J. Mega-Mix"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["F Slim","F. Slim","F.Slim","FBS","Faboy","Fat Boy","Fat Boy Slim","Fat Boy Slim 99","Fat Boy Slime","FatBoySlim","Fatbot Slim","Fatboy","Fatboy Alim","Fatboy Clim","Fatboy Fat","Fatboy Slime","FatboySlim","Fatboyslim","Slim","Slim Boy Fat","流線胖小子"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3101-Fatboy-Slim","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.fatboyslim.net/","https://www.facebook.com/fatboyslim","https://twitter.com/fatboyslim","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatboy_Slim","https://www.instagram.com/officialfatboyslim/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4534693/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4534693","image":"https://i.discogs.com/ZEvrBE2hSDLxhW19A9sw-TQlAoImEumrJF7UK2Nj-P8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:449/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ1MzQ2/OTMtMTQzOTM5Mzgx/OC00NDc0LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/6mjwt60rmMyYeIVY1pvWugRJ_u-Z1Z_ylKBR0GjOrCQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ1MzQ2/OTMtMTQzOTM5Mzgx/OC00NDc0LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"O$VMV$M is a duo made up of [a4213811] & [a3242219] bound to [a2877666] crew. Together they make sample based music woven together from B-movie horror films, old jungle/hardcore tapes and found/recorded sound. Heavily inspired by dub and its process of subtraction they often work backwards and strip away and warp elements until the original source material is barely recognisable.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4534693","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":2776918,"name":"Neek"},{"active":true,"id":3242219,"name":"Amos Childs"},{"active":true,"id":4213811,"name":"Sam Barrett (3)"}],"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4534693-OVMVM","type":"artist","urls":["https://osvmvsmosvmvsm.bandcamp.com/music","https://soundcloud.com/ovmvm"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4851206/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4851206","image":"https://i.discogs.com/HOneH1Gg7vtf4VLGIjCoe6y-AyHjHfPjOAcuN5pDOOs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:456/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ4NTEy/MDYtMTUyNTcwMzYx/Mi02MDkzLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/vDKTE3ZcBURKO5GhAb14HeFiEsrs-49GLLXXTDjw-wM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ4NTEy/MDYtMTUyNTcwMzYx/Mi02MDkzLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"[a2050797] is a London-based electronic musician and DJ. He was born in Hastings, England in 1979, but grew up on the boundary of East London and Essex, playing Drum & Bass on pirate radio in the mid nineties, most notably Rude FM. Having begun entrenched in London’s underground dance music scene his recordings eventually moved into a more freeform abstract compositional structure, drawing heavily from the early electronic masters as well as his background in pirate radio. In more recent years he has returned to his dance music roots, finally reconciling the disparate influences that have informed his music over the years to start afresh with a new project.\r\n\r\nIn 2014 he started the Basic Rhythm alias as a means of recontextualizing his dance music past, drawing directly upon his pirate radio years, while still pushing forward into new territories to emerge with more overtly dance floor material. Recorded primarily with the DJ in mind, his tracks are colourful, brutalist and adventurous contemporary hybrids, their angular rhythms drawing on Britain’s dance music past, but with an eye firmly on the present. He runs the [l1848549] record label.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4851206","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1413550,"name":"Imaginary Forces (2)"},{"id":2050797,"name":"Anthoney J Hart"},{"id":6201053,"name":"East Man"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4851206-Basic-Rhythm-2","type":"artist","urls":["https://basicrhythm.bandcamp.com","https://soundcloud.com/basicrhythm","http://www.entropyandenergy.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/645279/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"645279","image":"https://i.discogs.com/KLWir1qIaxbcyJ80JsZcbUH_HJIqpoOnXDaSV4fzTc4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:472/w:530/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY0NTI3/OS0xNDA1MjU4MjE5/LTY1NjEuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/FIJT9T_alhfYjFYRcyYmgUVPZDOExGTZIEbgkmeL2zk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY0NTI3/OS0xNDA1MjU4MjE5/LTY1NjEuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Grime / garage / dub producer from Manchester, UK.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:645279","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":4317487,"name":"John Goodwin (6)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Lil Chimpz"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/645279-Chimpo","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.myspace.com/feedthechimp"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/746170/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"746170","image":"https://i.discogs.com/CvOW9zisPZMitq2yOgnmvYfMTiGzo1jYpbs-VBg_4I0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:424/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc0NjE3/MC0xNjY4MjcxODU3/LTQzOTAuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/YxUuyaGyb8Ei4b-M_AEhLHm81b1Eeh6T_QiUIIZPjQo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc0NjE3/MC0xNjY4M